{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902568-making-of-a-spirit-talker","id":902568,"title":"Making of a spirit talker","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-29T01:40:33-07:00","id":902568,"title":"Making of a spirit talker","content":"As someone who is deeply in love with the animism parts of Idigan Chronicles (spirits and Shadow Realm) but doesn't particulary care about the Uratha themselves, I'd like to create/adapt a few supernatural merits for a &quot;shaman&quot; semitemplate, a mostly vanilla human who is in deep touch with the spirits and knows how to make deals with them ( or to coerce and drive away when necessary) .<br /> Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T01:43:16-07:00","id":902570,"title":"","content":"A wolf-blooded with the Horse tell (+ optional Piercing Eyes), the arcane armory merit, and sufficiently high attributes for summoning/abjuration/exorcism should cover the concept pretty thoroughly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T01:47:11-07:00","id":902571,"title":"","content":"Good. But I prefer to keep them humans (no wolf blooded, proximi or ghouls) and to develope some merits for social interactions with their spirits ( open Doors, discerning ranks or banes, honorary ranks in the Chorus, etc..).<br /> I am in favour of &quot;anyone can do it with the proper training, effort and sheer balls&quot; rather than &quot;because my daddy was a wolf&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-29-2016, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T02:02:42-07:00","id":902578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902568-making-of-a-spirit-talker?p=902571#post902571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good. But I prefer to keep them humans (no wolf blooded, proximi or ghouls) and to develope some merits for social interactions with their spirits ( open Doors, discerning ranks or banes, honorary ranks in the Chorus, etc..).<br /> I am in favour of &quot;anyone can do it with the proper training, effort and sheer balls&quot; rather than &quot;because my daddy was a wolf&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to ignore that Wolf-Blooded can spontaneously just happen (and aren't required to actually have any connection Uratha) and make it a matter of sheer training, I'm not sure where you'd start.<br /> <br /> Supernatural Merits aren't something you can get with hard work either. But anyone can perform abjurations, summonings, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T04:30:18-07:00","id":902620,"title":"","content":"Which books do you have access to? Do you want your Shamans modeled with CofD Corebook, Forsaken or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T04:47:19-07:00","id":902624,"title":"","content":"Mostly CofD. I want to make them mortal without powers on their own (except fetishes or boons from placated spirits) who specialize in abjuration, summonings, etc.. but with some merits as reflecting their training and experience (as mentioned adobe, opening doors in peaceful negotiations , gaining honorary ranks in a particular Chorus, etc...).<br /> Some of those merits could be accesible only to member of a spirit-focused cult or conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-29-2016, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T05:47:38-07:00","id":902646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902568-making-of-a-spirit-talker?p=902571#post902571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good. But I prefer to keep them humans (no wolf blooded, proximi or ghouls) and to develope some merits for social interactions with their spirits ( open Doors, discerning ranks or banes, honorary ranks in the Chorus, etc..).<br /> I am in favour of &quot;anyone can do it with the proper training, effort and sheer balls&quot; rather than &quot;because my daddy was a wolf&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too bad, you also lose access to rites. Y'know, what makes a shaman, well, a shaman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-29-2016, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T07:33:30-07:00","id":902707,"title":"","content":"The Merit you're looking for is Medium. They can create the appropriate base Conditions from scratch but must rely on the goodwill of the Spirits to cross over on their own. Automatic Writing is another Merit that could add some flavour to the character. There's a couple of Merits in the Hurt Locker spoilers that could help. Assertive Implement could stand in for a simple Fetish, there's an Invoke Spirit Merit that let's you summon a Rank 1 spirit, and there's the Hardened Exorcist Merit which adds your Occult Skill dots to your Integrity to calculate the bonuses to Abjuration, Summoning, and Exorcism.<br /> <br /> You might also want to look at the Skin Thief Merit from Dark Eras, since that one allows you to take on a spirit's form and powers. It's the closest to getting honorary Rank without being Uratha, a Spirit Mage, or one of the Purified.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Wolf-Blooded Tells and the Rites they grant access to are probably your best bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:33:57-07:00","id":902739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902568-making-of-a-spirit-talker?p=902707#post902707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Merit you're looking for is Medium. They can create the appropriate base Conditions from scratch but must rely on the goodwill of the Spirits to cross over on their own. Automatic Writing is another Merit that could add some flavour to the character. There's a couple of Merits in the Hurt Locker spoilers that could help. Assertive Implement could stand in for a simple Fetish, there's an Invoke Spirit Merit that let's you summon a Rank 1 spirit, and there's the Hardened Exorcist Merit which adds your Occult Skill dots to your Integrity to calculate the bonuses to Abjuration, Summoning, and Exorcism.<br /> <br /> You might also want to look at the Skin Thief Merit from Dark Eras, since that one allows you to take on a spirit's form and powers. It's the closest to getting honorary Rank without being Uratha, a Spirit Mage, or one of the Purified.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Wolf-Blooded Tells and the Rites they grant access to are probably your best bet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. I can work with that.<br /> <br /> Regarding honorary rank, I was thinking in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/698943-bowery-dogs-silver-syndicate\">Silver Syndicate</a> created by Lostlight:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 0- Congratulations! You got promotion! After long months of work in the company, you finally know the truth- that you don't just work with numbers of break legs, but also need to chase down spirits and hunt down werebeasts. Want too quite? Oh, too bad- you should have read the fine prints. At least you are not totally helpless. You may spend merit points on the Resonance Endowment.<br /> 000- you managed to survive that far! we can expect many great things from you! You get Contacts for 2 dots among criminal organizations. You also get an Honorary Rank of 1 while related to the Concrete Beasts's Choir (the group's totem).<br /> 00000- It seems that recruiting you was one good investment- and you are one among hundreds of happy costumers! It is time to get some of the profits back, right? You get Resources for 3 dots. Don't ask from where the money came. You don't want to know. You also get and Honorary Rank of 2 while relating to spirits of the Concrete Beast's Choir. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-29-2016, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T04:27:27-07:00","id":903388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902568-making-of-a-spirit-talker#post902568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you could buy book of spirits, it has multiple merits that you might be interested in.<br /> <br /> For communicating with spirits, it has Spirit Tongue.<br /> <br /> Easy Ride/Hollow Soul makes the character easier to possess, which could be used to bribe spirits. Hollow Soul allows spirits that don't even have the ability to possess possess you anyway.<br /> <br /> Pleasing Aura means that spirits like to flock to you and hang out basking in your aura.<br /> <br /> Residual Spirit Energy allows you to spill your blood and release Essence, which would be highly useful for bribing spirits.<br /> <br /> Locos Drinker allows a character to draw Essence out of a locus, but cannot store it by default- They could give it to a spirit in the area, or store it in a magic item that can store essence if they have such a thing, which could be used to bribe spirits.<br /> <br /> For communicating with spirits, once you basically share a language thanks to Spirit Tongue, social rolls.<br /> <br /> Coercion is a little more difficult, but Arcane Armory could be used to physically force a spirit to do something, if you have high combat skills, or use the blue book rules for exorcism and abjuration, which anyone can do.<br /> <br /> Or buy Second Sight, which is the book that has the thaumaturge template which specifically includes shamans as a magical tradition and convert all their merits into supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> Or borrow the favors system from the vampire section of Dark Eras, the covenant formed a favor network with all the supernaturals of britain, even including cosmic forces and saints and the like. Being a favor system, of course, be prepared to to return those favors in kind.<br /> <br /> Also, you know, there is no rule that social merits can't extend to supernatural groups. Retainer would be a bit much and I for one would put a cap on influence, but nothing wrong with allies- City Spirits of Chicago, or Contacts- Spirits of Knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 05-30-2016, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T04:35:41-07:00","id":903391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Or buy Second Sight</b>, which is the book that has the thaumaturge template which specifically includes shamans as a magical tradition and convert all their merits into supernatural merits. </div> </div> </div>.....<br /> (Facepalm)<br /> Or that, thank you, sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T04:52:04-07:00","id":903395,"title":"","content":"Glad to help, the writers of nwod/cofd have been kind enough to give us plenty of options to play with, it's generally a matter of finding an option you like.<br /> <br /> For example, I realized I forgot the options from Mirrors-<br /> <br /> 1) Forbidden Lore, meant to represent cthonic &quot;make a sanity check&quot; kind of magic, it has people basically buy their magical power with their own sanity. A shaman type who if they aren't careful will lose their ability to think like a human as they become more and more spirit like might be appealing.<br /> <br /> 2) Sorcery, which basically amounts to &quot;kick up the fantasy elements and let normal people buy supernatural powers.&quot; It sounds like you have werewolf second edition, so it would basically be &quot;normal people can use werewolf rituals&quot; if you so desired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T05:24:33-07:00","id":903408,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I made this post after reading <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits\">Sample Spirits</a>. I wanted a type of character focused in the direct interaction with those fellas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T19:38:59-07:00","id":903911,"title":"","content":"There's a Merit chain in Werewolf 2e core that might interest you from one of the hunting grounds...here, let me just quote it since it's a very niche thing in an easy-to-miss part of the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf 2e core, p.272</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">VOYAGER MEMBERSHIP<br /> This Merit reflects membership within a Voyager cult. With each progressive dot, the member gains an additional advantage.<br /> <br /> Initiate (\u2022): Initiates receive an Occult Specialty in Spirit Tongues. This allows them to understand and use rudimentary First Tongue. They can only communicate very simple ideas with their human mouths.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022): At this level, they gain a dot of Contacts, reflecting spirits they\u2019ve interacted with who inform them of the goings-on in the Hisil.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Minor leaders in the cult can feed their blood to spirits in the Hisil for Essence. For every point of lethal damage they suffer, they can offer one Essence to spirits; for each point of Essence so given they receive an extra die on all Social actions with that spirit for the following month.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): With this level, masters can open the Gauntlet with a few written and spoken words, and a volume of sacrificed blood. Roll Intelligence + Occult as an extended action; each roll requires one minute and a point of lethal damage. Success allows for one traveler to pass through the portal. Additional successes open the portal for an hour each, or make the portal allow one traveler access before closing.<br /> <br /> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The greatest Voyagers can use their words to generate Essence. They can spend Willpower instead of blood to create Essence; each point of Willpower creates 2 Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T20:23:44-07:00","id":903924,"title":"","content":"I most definitely missed this one, which is unfortunate because I love the elegance of Mystery Cult Initiations as a Merit. Done right, it can really flesh out a character or an organization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T00:16:17-07:00","id":904003,"title":"","content":"Question: how skilled can a human become with the First Tongue? Is difficult to be a shaman if you canon even talk to the spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T00:43:25-07:00","id":904017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902568-making-of-a-spirit-talker?p=904003#post904003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: how skilled can a human become with the First Tongue? Is difficult to be a shaman if you canon even talk to the spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>First Tongue is acquired via the Language: First Tongue merit in 2E. Although there's a lot of implication that humans can't speak it properly, there's nothing stopping them from taking the merit, so I'd say the rare few that do can be entirely fluent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T02:04:24-07:00","id":904048,"title":"","content":"I go with the Voyager method myself, but I admit I am not as heavily invested in the idea of mortals being as competent with spirits as you are. Given that I think most requests you would ask from spirits are fairly simple and that spirits are noted as often picking up local human languages, a lack of perfect fluency works for me. It gives dealing with spirits thos edge of weirdness and Otherness; besides, I'm willing to throw out highly intricate and involved conversations that I wasn't interested in having anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T03:36:18-07:00","id":904068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/902568-making-of-a-spirit-talker?p=904003#post904003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: how skilled can a human become with the First Tongue? Is difficult to be a shaman if you canon even talk to the spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In first edition, with the spirit tongue merit, anything beyond the dirt simple required successful skill rolls.<br /> <br /> As Inodiv pointed out, second edition doesn't give any such rules, so I guess do whatever feels right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:16:15-07:00","id":904130,"title":"","content":"In Werewolf it mentions that even though the Uratha can speak First Tongue, they do it with a noticeable accent. The Wolf-Blooded Tell that allows for speaking in First Tongue implies that it's virtually impossible for human vocal cords to even properly form all the sounds.<br /> <br /> Mage 2e elaborates on this a bit more, saying that Spirit Mages are given begrudging respect for their capabilities and they acknowledge the Honorary Rank Attainment, but they are outright offended by a Mage attempting to speak First Tongue.<br /> <br /> That being said, as mentioned above Spirits do pick up local human languages, and that seemed to work just fine in the Sundered World setting. The humans there interacted with Spirits frequently, often without any particular special talents, and it seemed to work out fairly well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:43:43-07:00","id":904141,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the First Tongue have a written form? A shaman might be a bit more fluent communicating that way. Rune-carved stones/tablets/circles/bones might not be for warding or &quot;magic&quot;, but rather simply more eloquent and specific communications to Spirits.<br /> <br /> The difference between grunting &quot;Please, no hurt&quot; and &quot;As per the agreements and pacts laid down in the Wreathhold Accords, I respectfully ask you not to bring willful harm upon those in this premises who obey the agreed upon Ban. Cordially yours, [Shaman].&quot;<br /> <br /> Sometimes politeness and courtesy are a magic all their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T23:27:38-07:00","id":904752,"title":"","content":"I don't remember if it was mentioned in second edition, but in first edition the spirit language could definitely be written down.<br /> <br /> In infinite macabre, the mysterious gates that allow for hyperspace travel, it's mentioned that the werewolves think the runes upon it are the language of the spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}